*heterogenuous effect of mass layoff by OOI on wages/search time
*using various controls

*Oren Danieli
*October 2020
*September 2021 - adding fixed effects
*tables 3, A2. Figures 2, A1

cap log close
log using ${log}\02_restud2_mass_layoffs.log, replace
set more off
set matsize 1000
est clear
fdzinstall estout

// load data for the layoff exercise
use $data/liab_OOI_layoffs.dta, clear
drop if X_age < 20

* as noted in paper, restrict mass layoff analysis to workers under age 55 (exclusive)
drop if X_age > 54

* people with missing OOI as we can't use them in the analysis
drop if missing(OOI)

* drop people who did not have a job before (daily wage <1 euro)
drop tentgelt_gr
drop if tentgelt <1

gen income0 = tentgelt

*sum by worker (not worker-month observation)
preserve 
	collapse (mean) X_* year income* pre* tenure, by (persnr)
	summ X_* year income* pre*
	tab X_schule
	qui summ tenure, detail
restore

*change tenure to be 0 at median
gen demed_ten = tenure - r(p50)

*change age to be 0 at 40 
gen age40 = X_age-40

* keep the variables we want
keep persnr  tentgelt demed_ten X_frau X_schule age40 X_german ///
	year OOI betnr income* X_past_occ* pre_* part_time*

* reshape to long format
	// note: month is not 1-12.
reshape long income pre_income part_time, i(persnr year) j(month)

*separate pre trends to separate observations
expand 2, gen(pre)
replace month = - month if pre
replace income = pre_income if pre
drop pre_income

*bin by month and establishment
egen emp_month = group(betnr month)

*set month 0 to 100 to avoid negatives
replace month = month + 100

******
*Relative Income
*******

*look at relative income to income before layoff
gen rel_inc = income/tentgelt

*raw trend (appendix figure)
areg rel_inc ib(100).month, a(betnr) cluster (persnr)

*look at the coefficient for OOI (figure)
areg rel_inc ib(100).month##c.OOI, a(emp_month) cluster(persnr)

*employment figure
gen any_inc = income>0
replace any_inc = . if missing(income)
areg any_inc ib(100).month##c.OOI, a(emp_month) cluster(persnr)

*stuff for R1:
*figures with controls 
areg rel_inc ib(100).month##c.OOI c.month##c.month##c.month##c.demed_ten##c.demed_ten c.month##c.month##c.month##c.age40##c.age40 c.month##c.month##c.month##i.X_frau c.month##c.month##c.month##ib(6).X_schule c.month##c.month##c.month##c.X_past_occ*, a(emp_month) cluster(persnr)

areg any_inc ib(100).month##c.OOI c.month##c.month##c.month##c.demed_ten##c.demed_ten c.month##c.month##c.month##c.age40##c.age40 c.month##c.month##c.month##i.X_frau c.month##c.month##c.month##ib(6).X_schule c.month##c.month##c.month##c.X_past_occ*, a(emp_month) cluster(persnr)

*figure with part time
gen emp_or_part = any_inc
replace emp_or_part = 0.5 if (part_time==1)

gen emp_no_part = any_inc
replace emp_no_part = 0 if (part_time==1)
areg emp_no_part ib(100).month##c.OOI, a(emp_month) cluster(persnr)


*change back
replace month = month - 100
drop if month <0

*additional controls (for table)
areg rel_inc i.month##c.OOI, a(emp_month) cluster(persnr)
eststo
areg rel_inc i.month##c.OOI c.month##c.month##c.month##c.demed_ten##c.demed_ten, a(emp_month) cluster(persnr)
eststo
areg rel_inc i.month##c.OOI c.month##c.month##c.month##c.demed_ten##c.demed_ten c.month##c.month##c.month##c.age40##c.age40 c.month##c.month##c.month##i.X_frau c.month##c.month##c.month##ib(6).X_schule, a(emp_month) cluster(persnr)
eststo
areg rel_inc i.month##c.OOI c.month##c.month##c.month##c.demed_ten##c.demed_ten c.month##c.month##c.month##c.age40##c.age40 c.month##c.month##c.month##i.X_frau c.month##c.month##c.month##ib(6).X_schule c.month##c.month##c.month##c.X_past_occ*, a(emp_month) cluster(persnr)
eststo

esttab, se replace star(* 0.10 ** 0.05 *** 0.01) keep(3.month#c.OOI 6.month#c.OOI 12.month#c.OOI 24.month#c.OOI )
est clear

********
*Search time
*******

areg any_inc i.month##c.OOI, a(emp_month) cluster(persnr)
eststo
areg any_inc i.month##c.OOI c.month##c.month##c.month##c.demed_ten##c.demed_ten, a(emp_month) cluster(persnr)
eststo
areg any_inc i.month##c.OOI c.month##c.month##c.month##c.demed_ten##c.demed_ten c.month##c.month##c.month##c.age40##c.age40 c.month##c.month##c.month##i.X_frau c.month##c.month##c.month##ib(6).X_schule, a(emp_month) cluster(persnr)
eststo
areg any_inc i.month##c.OOI c.month##c.month##c.month##c.demed_ten##c.demed_ten c.month##c.month##c.month##c.age40##c.age40 c.month##c.month##c.month##i.X_frau c.month##c.month##c.month##ib(6).X_schule c.month##c.month##c.month##c.X_past_occ*, a(emp_month) cluster(persnr)
eststo

esttab, se replace star(* 0.10 ** 0.05 *** 0.01) keep(3.month#c.OOI 6.month#c.OOI 12.month#c.OOI 24.month#c.OOI )
est clear


log close
